  "question": {
    "text": "The time period of oscillations of a block attached to a spring is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When the spring is replaced by another spring, the time period of the block is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If both the springs are connected in series and the block is made to oscillate using the combination, then the time period of the block is",
